# AEM Demo Page

Set up one demo page per component, configure it, and capture the dialog (only when it changed) and the author preview. Output: `demo/demo-page.md` in the story's spec dir, read by `/dx-doc-gen` and `/dx-qa-handoff`.

## How to use

```
@AEMDemoPage hero --local
@AEMDemoPage 12345
```

## Configuration

Read `.ai/config.yaml` for `aem.author-url`, `aem.author-url-qa`, `aem.publish-url-qa`, `aem.component-path`, `aem.component-prefix`, `aem.demo-parent-path`, `scm.base-branch`, `scm.org`, `scm.project`.

## Steps

Follow the `aem-demo-page` skill (`skills/aem-demo-page/SKILL.md` in the dx-aem plugin) node by node:

1. **Instance** — `--local` → local author; otherwise QA. Every AEM call passes `instance: "<local|qa>"`.
2. **Component** — from arguments, else `implement.md` / `explain.md` in the spec dir.
3. **Other repo ready?** — when `explain.md` / `research.md` list another required repo whose change the page depends on, stop until it is deployed (local: deployed by hand; QA: its PR on the work item is completed): "Cross-repo dependency — <repo> must be deployed first".
4. **Dialog changed?** — the change touches `<component>/_cq_dialog/`, or the component is new.
5. **Deploy gate (QA)** — repo dialog fields must exist on QA; otherwise stop: "Not deployed to QA yet".
6. **Page** — reuse the best existing page with the component; create under `aem.demo-parent-path` only for a new component. On QA, try the page path from the local run first.
7. **Configure** — real authored values first; mock only new fields with no data. Never change a reused production page.
8. **Screenshots** — authenticate with `bash .ai/lib/aem-playwright-auth.sh author <local|qa>` and load the storage state; dialog via the Granite editor API (only when changed), preview at `<author><page>.html?wcmmode=disabled`. Save to `demo/<local|qa>/`.
9. **Upload (QA)** — `bash .ai/lib/upload-attachment.sh --org … --project … --id <id> --file … --name <id>-<file>`.
10. **Write `demo/demo-page.md`** — replace only this environment's block.

## Rules

- One instance per run; never mix local and QA.
- Reuse pages for existing components; create only for new ones.
- Read every URL and path from config.
